      "content": "Climate of West Bengal"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "West Bengal experiences a tropical monsoon climate characterized by hot, humid summers and mild winters.",
        "The vegetation transitions from alpine and sub-tropical forests in the northern Himalayas to tidal mangrove forests in the southern delta.",
        "The Sundarbans represents the largest mangrove forest ecosystem in the world and serves as a critical habitat for the Royal Bengal Tiger.",
        "Key wildlife protected areas include Gorumara and Jaldapara for the One-Horned Rhinoceros, and Singalila for the Red Panda."
      ],
      "id": "zb7u7pu"
    },
